---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe13.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Provisions — Recognition Criteria" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Contingent Liabilities — Disclosed, Not Recognised" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Contingent Assets — Never Recognised" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. Measurement — Best Estimate" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Discounting Where the Time Value of Money Is Material" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Common Provisions in Practice" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — Recognising a Warranty Provision" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Worked Example — a Contingent Liability, Disclosed Only" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Relationship to IAS 37" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s16", label: "16. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A three-part framework for uncertain obligations and rights</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 13 governs PROVISIONS, CONTINGENT LIABILITIES, and CONTINGENT ASSETS — DESPITE its SHORTER title ("CONTINGENCIES," RATHER than IAS 37's FULLER "Provisions, CONTINGENT Liabilities and CONTINGENT Assets"), this STANDARD covers ESSENTIALLY the SAME three-part FRAMEWORK, BROADLY converged with IAS 37 internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Uncertain obligations and possible rights arising from past events</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies to UNCERTAIN present OBLIGATIONS (PROVISIONS and CONTINGENT liabilities) and POSSIBLE rights (CONTINGENT assets) ARISING from PAST events, WHERE the TIMING or AMOUNT of ANY resulting OUTFLOW or INFLOW REMAINS uncertain.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Provisions — Recognition Criteria</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A present obligation, a probable outflow, and a reliable estimate</div><div class="check-list"><span>A present obligation (legal or constructive) exists as a result of a past event</span><span>It is probable that an outflow of economic benefits will be required to settle the obligation</span><span>A reliable estimate can be made of the amount of the obligation</span></div>
<div class="note">ALL THREE criteria must be MET for a PROVISION to be RECOGNISED — CONSISTENT with IAS 37's OWN recognition FRAMEWORK internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Contingent Liabilities — Disclosed, Not Recognised</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Possible obligations, or obligations that aren't probable or reliably measurable</div><div class="text-supporting">A CONTINGENT LIABILITY — a POSSIBLE obligation WHOSE existence will be CONFIRMED only by FUTURE uncertain EVENTS, or a PRESENT obligation that is EITHER not PROBABLE or CANNOT be reliably MEASURED — is NOT recognised on the BALANCE Sheet, but IS disclosed in the NOTES (UNLESS the possibility of an OUTFLOW is REMOTE).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Contingent Assets — Never Recognised</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Disclosed only where an inflow is probable</div><div class="text-supporting">A CONTINGENT ASSET — a POSSIBLE asset WHOSE existence will be CONFIRMED only by FUTURE uncertain EVENTS — is NEVER recognised (AVOIDING the RECOGNITION of income that MAY never MATERIALISE), but IS disclosed in the NOTES WHERE an INFLOW of economic BENEFITS is PROBABLE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Measurement — Best Estimate</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">The best estimate of expenditure required to settle the obligation</div><div class="text-supporting">A PROVISION is MEASURED at the BEST ESTIMATE of the EXPENDITURE REQUIRED to SETTLE the PRESENT obligation at the REPORTING date — CONSIDERING the RISKS and UNCERTAINTIES SURROUNDING the underlying EVENTS and CIRCUMSTANCES.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Discounting Where the Time Value of Money Is Material</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Present-valuing long-dated obligations</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE the EFFECT of the TIME value of MONEY is MATERIAL (TYPICALLY for LONGER-dated OBLIGATIONS), the PROVISION amount is the PRESENT value of the EXPENDITURES EXPECTED to be REQUIRED to SETTLE the obligation — CONSISTENT with IAS 37's OWN discounting requirement internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Common Provisions in Practice</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recurring examples across Chinese enterprises</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Product warranty provisions</span><span>Onerous contract provisions</span><span>Restructuring provisions</span><span>Litigation and legal claim provisions</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Recognising a Warranty Provision</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Estimating future warranty repair costs</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A manufacturer's product warranty obligation</div><div class="wk-body">A manufacturer sells RMB 100,000,000 of products during the year, each carrying a 2-year warranty. Based on historical experience, the company estimates warranty repair costs will amount to 2% of sales.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognises a WARRANTY PROVISION of RMB 100,000,000 × 2% = <strong>RMB 2,000,000</strong>, since a PRESENT obligation EXISTS (from the SALES already MADE), an OUTFLOW is PROBABLE, and a RELIABLE estimate CAN be made based on HISTORICAL experience.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — a Contingent Liability, Disclosed Only</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A possible obligation that doesn't yet meet the recognition threshold</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: An ongoing, uncertain legal dispute</div><div class="wk-body">A company is a defendant in a lawsuit seeking RMB 15,000,000 in damages. Legal counsel advises that the outcome is genuinely uncertain, with the likelihood of an adverse outcome assessed as possible, but not probable.</div><div class="wk-answer">Since an ADVERSE outcome is NOT considered PROBABLE, the company does NOT recognise a PROVISION, but DOES disclose the NATURE of the CONTINGENT LIABILITY, an ESTIMATE of its POTENTIAL financial EFFECT, and the UNCERTAINTIES involved, WITHIN the notes to the financial STATEMENTS.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 13 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Carrying amount of provisions at the beginning and end of the period, and movements during the period</span><span>Nature of contingent liabilities and, where practicable, an estimate of their financial effect</span><span>Nature of contingent assets, where an inflow is probable</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether an outflow of economic benefits is genuinely probable, distinguishing a provision from a mere contingent liability</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Best estimate of the expenditure required to settle a recognised obligation</span><span>Discount rate applied to long-dated provisions</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 37</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 13 vs IAS 37</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 13</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 37</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Provision recognition criteria</span><span>Same three-part test</span><span>Same three-part test — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Contingent liabilities/assets</span><span>Disclosed only, not recognised</span><span>Disclosed only, not recognised — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard — the SHORTER title is a NAMING difference RATHER than a SUBSTANTIVE one.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every contingency-related event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Provision recognised</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Liability and expense recognised</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Contingent liability/asset</span><span>Notes only</span><span>No Balance Sheet or Income Statement recognition</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 8</span><span>Impairment of Assets — a related, but distinct, form of asset-side uncertainty, addressed separately from this Standard's liability-side focus</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Provision</div><div class="glossary-def">A liability of uncertain timing or amount, recognised when a present obligation exists, an outflow is probable, and a reliable estimate can be made.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Contingent liability</div><div class="glossary-def">A possible obligation whose existence depends on future uncertain events, or a present obligation that is not probable or not reliably measurable — disclosed but not recognised.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe13 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
